==Trivia==
*Each Cats in the Snow stage's Japanese name is a reference to a different song:
**[[Langue de Chat|Stage 1]]: Shiroi Henjintachi ("White Weirdos") = "[https://youtu.be/pvqvBAA-0AE Shiroi Koibitotachi] ("White Lovers") by [[wikipedia:Keisuke Kuawata|Keisuke Kuawata]]
**[[White Dove|Stage 2]]: White Dove = "[https://youtu.be/xdnDrHWmiic White Love]" by [[wikipedia:Speed (Japanese band)|Speed]]
**[[Snow at Dawn|Stage 3]]: Naguri Yuki ("Violent Snow") = "[https://youtu.be/FwXluXjBaqw Nagori Yuki]" ("Unseasonal Snow") by [[wikipedia:ja:イルカ (歌手)|Iruka]]
**[[Buddha of Romance|Stage 4]]: Romance no Hotokesama ("Buddha of Romance") = "[https://youtu.be/T8yZWCg85Cs Romance no Kamisama] ("Cupid of Romance") by [[wikipedia:Kohmi Hirose|Kohmi Hirose]]
**[[Icy Desire|Stage 5]]: Gerende ga Tokeru Hodo Koi Shitai ("A Dead Body so in Love That it Melts the Slopes") = "[https://youtu.be/MRfnpEf54eM Gerente ga Tokeru Hodo Koishitai] ("I Want to Fall so in Love That it Melts the Slopes") by Kohmi Hirose
***Kohmi Hirose is the only musical artist to get more than one reference in this event.
***It is one of the three events to have such a naming scheme, the others being [[Never Summer! (Monthly Event)|Never Summer!]] and [[Never Not Summer! (Monthly Event)|Never Not Summer!]].

